I did some more testing with original NetHack 3.4.3, and got
the following results, where S4, S2, S3, S1 represent inside,
free-square, door-square, and outside.  I tried canceling both
blessed oil and blessed restore-ability I'd just bought:

Item          Cancel       Shopkeeper
Descr:        Location:    Angry?
Blessed Oil   S4           No   (no bug)
Blessed Oil   S3           No   (no bug)
Blessed Oil   S2           No   (no bug)
Blessed Oil   S1           No   (no bug)
Blessed R.A.  S4           No   (no bug)
Blessed R.A.  S3           Yes! (bug)
Blessed R.A.  S2           Yes! (bug)
Blessed R.A.  S1           No   (no bug)

Oddly, this bug exists only with water-based potions, not
oil-based potions!

Also, it exists only on the free square and in the door.
The shopkeeper does NOT get angry if you cancel a blessed
water-based potion you just bought while DEEPLY inside
the store.  (But he does offer to buy it from you when you
drop it there, unlike when you drop it on S3, S2, or S1.)

After applying your patch:

 case OBJ_FLOOR:
  objroom = *in_rooms(obj->ox, obj->oy, SHOPBASE);
  shkp = shop_keeper(objroom);
  if (!shkp || !inhishop(shkp)) return;
#if defined O_DWYER_PATCH
  if (!costly_spot(obj->ox, obj->oy)) return; /* A.J. O'Dwyer */
#endif
  if (costly_spot(u.ux, u.uy) && objroom == *u.ushops) {
      Norep("You cancel it, you pay for it!");
      bill_dummy_object(obj);
  } else
      (void) stolen_value(obj, obj->ox, obj->oy, FALSE, FALSE);
